OL,3,GNEWSAPark tree collapse caused by
OL,4,Afungal infection
OL,5,
OL,6,FA 131-year-old oak tree that recently
OL,7,Fcollapsed in Peckham Rye Park was
OL,8,Fbrought down by a fungal infection,
OL,9,Faccording to Southwark Council, but
OL,10,Finvestigations continue into whether
OL,11,Fpersistent waterlogging in the area
OL,12,Fplayed a role.
OL,14,FThe south London council said the tree
OL,15,Fwas infected with Ganoderma applanatum,
OL,16,Fa fungus that causes unrecoverable
OL,17,Fdecay in a tree's roots and lower
OL,18,Ftrunk.
OL,23,APub: 21-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
